    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0303" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v19/pg271"/>

                <head>126. Telegram From the Embassy in Poland to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="0" xml:id="d126-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Warsaw</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-09-25T19:00:00+02:00">September 25,
                            1958, 7 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>476. USUN for Lodge. Beam–Wang Talks. Comments today’s meeting: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Wang’s position continues hard and unyielding. He shows no disposition
                            make concessions to US viewpoint which would be required if real
                            negotiation to result.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Wang gave impression of man marking time. His presentation was a
                            strong but routine recapitulation ChiCom position. Not only produced
                            nothing new himself but made no effort probe US intentions. Neither did
                            he accuse US of stalling or otherwise attempt pressure US to come up
                            with new proposals. In response our expression preference for morning
                            meeting time he preferred Tuesday to Monday.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Wang’s reference to US press not supporting government’s position may
                            be significant. Although could be merely convenient debating point might
                            also mean ChiCom’s are confident opposition to US military intervention
                            both within US and among allies may effectively prevent such
                            intervention.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Beam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d126-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d126-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.93/9–2558. Secret; Niact; Limit
                    Distribution. Received at 2:26 p.m. Repeated priority to USUN and niact to
                    Taipei.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
